    "raw": "Given:\n- 40% of the class are boys.\n- The rest (60%) are girls.\n- Boys score 80% on the test.\n- Girls score 90% on the test.\n\nTo find the class average, we use the weighted average formula:\n\\[ \\text{Class Average} = (\\text{Percentage of Boys} \\times \\text{Boys' Score}) + (\\text{Percentage of Girls} \\times \\text{Girls' Score}) \\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\\[ \\text{Class Average} = (0.40 \\times 80) + (0.60 \\times 90) \\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\\[ 0.40 \\times 80 = 32 \\]\n\\[ 0.60 \\times 90 = 54 \\]\n\nAdding these together:\n\\[ 32 + 54 = 86 \\]\n\nSo, the class average on the test is 86.\n\nFINAL: 86",
